<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tiantishan Grottoes</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">5th century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tiantishan Grottoes are Buddhist cave temples near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wuwei">Wuwei</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gansu">Gansu</a> province, north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. They were begun in the early 5th century under the Northern Liang ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juqu-mengxun">Juqu Mengxun</a> and are among the earliest Buddhist cave temples in China. Many of their sculptures and murals were moved to the Gansu Provincial Museum when a reservoir was built below the caves in the 1950s.</p></div>
